thematics?": "PCA reduces dimensions by identifying axes (principal components) where variance is highest. Start with *X’ = X − mean(X)* to standardize data. Compute covariance matrix, diagonalize it, and take top eigenvectors. The math feels complex only at first—my extraversion helps me break it into parts like a recipe. It’s iterative, not intimidating if I step back!", "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations (e.g., explaining calculus via real-world physics analogies for students who dislike abstract terms). They’d also debug mistakes instantly—like my videogame tutorials do—but I’d want teachers to guide the discovery process, blending AI’s speed with human curiosity. Think ‘AI as a co-pilot.’"
